ages/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Vision\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Vision\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Capricious Thief\"><img alt=\"Capricious Thief\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"+1 KP when conditions met\"><img alt=\"+1 KP when conditions met\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/0/0d/Dissicon_ff2_Fir1.png/revision/latest?cb=20110126024837\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Assist Character\"><img alt=\"Assist Character\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Dissicon ff2 Fir1.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissicon_ff2_Fir1.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/0/0d/Dissicon_ff2_Fir1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20110126024837\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/44/DFF_Summonstone.png/revision/latest?cb=20100712153022\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Leviathan (AUTO)\"><img alt=\"Leviathan (AUTO)\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"38\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Summonstone.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Summonstone.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/44/DFF_Summonstone.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20100712153022\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Ah, the perfect place for that KP Gambler we got in the last chapter! Multichain at D3 with the KP Gambler to chain all five enemies and get a nice 75 KP. Use that Soundwave skill if you like, might as well, it's just gonna take up space in your skill menu better used for a Charge skill. The bonus line is 5 and the KP Chance is a 90 second win, especially easy if you use Soundwave. There's a boss at the end to try and get that EX Gauge up.\n</p><p>First up is a Fleeting Flash with Launch, Smite and Aerora. Next a Capricious Thief with Scoop Art and Strom Impulse, the aerial forward spin attack. Now the three Hard enemies, a Capricious Thief with Scoop Art and Solution 9, the Hyper Ring set-up, and Cagnazzo. Next, an Ephemeral Phantom with Jecht's ground combo, aerial Jecht Block, the Hyper Ring, and Scarmiglione. Last is an Ephemeral Vision with Sphere Shot, Hop Step, that Hyper Ring, and Cagnazzo. Soundwave makes already simple and easy fights even simpler and easier here.\n</p><p>The summonstone is the auto version of Leviathan, as you know from seeing enemies use it, it summons automatically when the opponent Breaks you and saps their Bravery by increments of 50 every other second or so for a period of time. It's useless, the only time opponents will be Breaking you is in Confessions of the Creator, by which time we can get the manual version of Leviathan which drains more Bravery than the auto version.\n</p><p>As we approach the end piece, Tidus tells Firion to go on ahead, for some really dumb reason. So of course we're without an Assist now, change boosters to Empty Assist Gauge appropriately. This is a continuity snarl from the original Dissidia, where they actually split up before this gateway, so here it made sense for Tidus to call out for Firion. Jecht arrives to fight, but the Emperor appears and tells Jecht that it's too early for the final boss now, so Jecht takes off while the Emperor gives Tidus a way to vent in liu of the old man.\n</p>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Emperor_Mateus_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Emperor Mateus (Dissidia PSP)\">The Emperor</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/88/EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20110216231129\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"EmperorDissidiaRender\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"91\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-image-key=\"EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/88/EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/91?cb=20110216231129\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">2,944\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">18\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">550\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Bombard, Thunder Crest, Light Crest, Mine, Dynamite\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Flare, Starfall\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Atomos\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">2/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The difficulty of this battle is directly proportional to if you charged up your EX Gauge or not before coming here. The Emperor has all the same tricks as before, but this time you're in his domain, the wide-open spaces of Dream's End and the Empyreal Paradox are gone. Here in Pandaemonium his spells take up half the hallways, his projectiles bounce like mad and interrupt your attacks, and in general the tight confines make it hard to avoid his traps. He's got five Blue Gems boosting his Base Bravery to 550 by default, and factor in he's probably got at <i>least</i> a dozen levels on you, maybe more, and he can blast you into hell with only a few attacks while also being very hard to Break. Remember to use Energy Rain to deflect Flare when you can, but avoid Spiral Cut since it has you move on start-up so if you mistime it Tidus will jump right into the flame and get hit. His summon Atomos sucks your Bravery out and gives it to him when you land an HP hit, but he seemed picky about using it and didn't do so until late in the fight when it didn't make much difference.\n</p><p>The reason the fight's difficulty depends on how much you built up your EX Gauge is because of Tidus's EX Mode bonus. It's the same as Cloud's bonus, he wields the Caladbolg and gets its benefit of doing up to twice as much damage as usual depending on his HP, along with the critical hit rate going up. Without EX Mode you're going to have to whittle the Emperor down, barring your Cactuar summon doing it for you one time, and he will do a lot of damage to you with ease. But with EX Mode a single Full Slide or Sonic Buster will Break him, and you can quickly rack up the Bravery needed to finish him off. As for Tidus's other EX Mode benefits, let's take care of them while on the topic, he runs faster and deflects low-priority projectiles while running, and his dodging attacks make him invincible longer while dodging. His EX Burst isn't too hard, stop the cursor as close to the center as you can, you have enough time to let it make a couple passes while you pin down the timing of the cursor movement. Don't underestimate its damage just because the first few hits are weak, my Level 5 Tidus did 600 Bravery damage on the last hit alone, the Burst's power is all in that final hit so it is crucial you nail it right.\n</p><p>As the fight ends, the Emperor blasts Tidus with a shock of electricity and vanishes with a laugh, mocking that hatred won't get him his Crystal.\n</p><p>On the world map now, we're still alone. On the world map follow the path to reach Crescent Lake.  By the shore there's an Imitation Despot to take down, and a Maser Eye in a chest beyond it. The chest on the island has a Pink Tail. Now there's just the blue gateway to check out.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"1000 gil\"><img alt=\"1000 gil\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204000919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Capricious Thief\"><img alt=\"Capricious Thief\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"17\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Strange Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ae/DFF_Strange_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/17?cb=20110204000919\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgc